   120	# a printed PENDING line. The mechanism exists for mid-session freezes of
   121	# Gate-1 cache-stable files (CLAUDE.md §0), where a re-statement must land at
   122	# a closeout rather than mid-flight; a pending site is also excluded from the
   123	# cross-doc equality pool so the frozen value cannot drag other docs down.
   124	# The registry is EMPTY today: its one historical entry (CLAUDE.md
   125	# tests=13000, frozen during the PLAN-166 W0 session) was CONSUMED when
   126	# commit 65daff0 restated CLAUDE.md to "~14,000 parametrized cases" — and
   127	# keeping the entry past the restatement would have permanently grandfathered
   128	# the exact stale value (a revert to "~13,000" exited 0, because the pending
   129	# lookup runs BEFORE the band check; found by the W0 adversarial re-pass).
   130	# Rules for any future entry:
   131	#   - key on doc + metric + the EXACT frozen value; any OTHER out-of-band
   132	#     figure at the site stays a hard violation;
   133	#   - DELETE the entry in the same commit that lands the restatement — the
   134	#     exemption is not self-clearing against reverts of that restatement;
   135	#   - it prints on every single run, so it cannot rot unnoticed.
   136	#
   137	# NOTE on the two glob-ambiguous / underivable numbers (code-reviewer P2):
   138	#   - "_lib modules" is pinned to the TOP-LEVEL `_lib/*.py` glob (68). The
   139	#     recursive `_lib/**/*.py` count (incl. adapters/ + subdirs) is larger
   140	#     (~140); docs must state the top-level number to match this gate.
   141	#   - "registered hooks" (46) = distinct `*.py` script basenames appearing in
   142	#     command strings of the settings.json hooks{} SUBTREE, parsed as JSON
   143	#     (matches the hook_live_smoke check). S287: the old whole-file grep with
   144	#     a hyphenless regex captured the statusLine `statusline-ceo.py` as a
   145	#     phantom `ceo.py` (47). This is distinct from "hook .py files on disk"
   146	#     (57) — some on-disk hooks are not wired into settings.json — and from
   147	#     "registrations" (48): total hook ENTRIES incl. non-.py commands (one
   148	#     script can fire on several events).
   149	#
   150	# RULE-LIVENESS CONTRACT (S287 vacuous-gate lesson): a metric whose regexes
   151	# match ZERO watched docs reports "no drift" with a number nobody checks —
   152	# a dead gate. The per-metric match count is exported as `rule_matches` in
   153	# --json, and the real-repo test suite asserts every doc-gated metric
   154	# matches >=1 site (test_verify_counts.py). Synthetic test trees are exempt
   155	# by construction (the assertion lives in the real-repo test, not here).
   156	# The historical "6 core hooks" enumeration in CLAUDE.md is a labelled
   157	# historical subset, NOT a live total — it is not gated here.
   158	# ============================================================================
   159	#
   160	# Bash 3.2 portable (macOS default). Doc-parsing delegated to a stdlib-only
   161	# python3 block (python3 is already required for the test-collect step).
   162	
   163	set -euo pipefail
   164	
   165	REPO_ROOT="${VERIFY_COUNTS_ROOT:-$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../../.." && pwd)}"
   166	
   167	QUIET=0
   168	JSON=0
   169	NO_TESTS=0
   170	for arg in "$@"; do
   171	  case "$arg" in
   172	    --quiet)    QUIET=1 ;;
   173	    --json)     JSON=1 ;;
   174	    --no-tests) NO_TESTS=1 ;;
   175	    -h|--help)
   176	      # Usage + the full COUNT/APPROX contract. Keep this range in sync with
   177	      # the header: it ends at the line before "NOTE on the two
   178	      # glob-ambiguous" (S294 — the old '2,75p' truncated mid-sentence once
   179	      # the APPROX CONTRACT block landed).
   180	      sed -n "2,$(( $(grep -n '^# NOTE on the two glob-ambiguous' "$0" | head -1 | cut -d: -f1) - 1 ))p" "$0"
   181	      exit 0
   182	      ;;
   183	    *)
   184	      echo "verify-counts.sh: unknown arg: $arg" >&2
   185	      exit 2
   186	      ;;
   187	  esac
   188	done
