SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:478:| `fact_gate_activation_changed` (v2.48) | `action`, `hook` (str — bounded identifier token, producer = `check_bash_safety`), `enabled` (bool — coerced), `source` (str — CLOSED enum: `settings` / `env_emergency_off` / `sota_master_off` / `default_advisory`; coerced to `default_advisory`), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-154 item 6 A8 / ADR-160 D5 (2026-07-10) — HMAC governance event on every OBSERVED ADVISORY↔ENFORCE flip of the fact-forcing deny-once gate (settings-backed `CEO_FACT_GATE_ENFORCE`; env form is emergency-off ONLY). Detection is lazy (hooks are per-invocation processes): the last observed state persists in the per-session fact-gate state file and is compared on the next already-matched destructive command. Routes through `_FACT_GATE_ACTIVATION_CHANGED_ALLOWLIST` scrub, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: command bytes, settings-file contents. NO ATLAS technique. |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:482:| `codex_tool_recorded` (v2.49) | `action`, `harness` (str — CLOSED enum: `codex`; coerced), `hook_event_name` (str — CLOSED enum: `PostToolUse`; coerced), `tool_name_enum` (str — CLOSED enum: `Bash` / `Edit` / `Write` / `Task` / `Read` / `MultiEdit` / `NotebookEdit` / `Glob` / `Grep` / `WebFetch` / `WebSearch` / `mcp_other` / `other`; the codex host adapter aliases `apply_patch`→`Write`/`Edit` and `spawn_agent`→`Task` upstream, `audit_log._codex_tool_enum` folds `mcp__*`→`mcp_other`, and any residual off-enum value coerces to `other`), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-155 Wave 4-A / ADR-161 (2026-07-10) — per-tool-call append for the OpenAI-Codex PostToolUse `*` matcher, emitted by `audit_log.py` under `CEO_HOOK_ADAPTER=codex`. DISTINCT from the claude-only `agent_spawn` rail and from `tool_call_lifecycle_recorded`, so codex-completeness analysis can count the per-tool rail separately from the turn-level backstop. Typed emitter `emit_codex_tool_recorded`; routes through the dedicated deny-by-default `_CODEX_TOOL_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + VALUE re-coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: command bytes, `apply_patch` body, file paths, `tool_response` text, prompt. **Completeness residual (named):** partial shell interception means a per-tool row may be ABSENT — absence is not evidence of absence of activity; the HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` are unchanged (append-only). NO ATLAS technique (governance/observability breadcrumb). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:484:| `grok_tool_recorded` (v2.50) | `action`, `harness` (str — CLOSED enum: `grok`; coerced), `hook_event_name` (str — CLOSED enum: `PostToolUse`; coerced), `tool_name_enum` (str — CLOSED enum: `Bash` / `Edit` / `Write` / `Task` / `Read` / `MultiEdit` / `NotebookEdit` / `Glob` / `Grep` / `WebFetch` / `WebSearch` / `mcp_other` / `other`; the grok host adapter aliases `run_terminal_command`→`Bash`, `search_replace`→`Edit`, `spawn_subagent`→`Task` upstream, `audit_log._grok_tool_enum` folds `mcp__*`→`mcp_other`, residual off-enum → `other`), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-156 Wave 4 / ADR-162 (2026-07-12) — per-tool-call append for the xAI Grok Build PostToolUse event, emitted by `audit_log.py` under `CEO_HOOK_ADAPTER=grok`. DISTINCT from the codex/claude rails. Typed emitter `emit_grok_tool_recorded`; dedicated deny-by-default `_GROK_TOOL_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + VALUE re-coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: command bytes, edit body, file paths, `toolResult` text, prompt. **Completeness residual (named):** grok's hook coverage is per-event and PostToolUse is passive there — absence of a row is not evidence of absence of activity; the HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` are unchanged (append-only). NO ATLAS technique. |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:488:| `pair_rail_review_expected` (v2.52) | `action`, `tool_name` (str — CLOSED enum: `Edit` / `Write` / `MultiEdit` / `NotebookEdit` / `unknown`; off-enum COERCED to `unknown`), `file_path_hash_prefix` (str — 16-hex SHA-256 prefix of target file path, the SAME token/helper as `pair_rail_case`; bounded shape `[0-9a-f]{0,16}`, off-shape COERCED to empty; raw path forbidden per LLM06 side-channel guard; r4 F2, retained as the LEGACY fallback bucket key + harmless secondary key — id-less events still pair per (session, file-hash) BUCKET), `review_id` (str — exact-shape `([0-9a-f]{16})?` (EXACTLY 16 lowercase hex, or empty; r6 F2: raw value validated, off-shape incl. oversize DROPPED to empty — never truncated); r5 F2 — THE invocation correlation key: minted per review entry by `_decide()` (`os.urandom(8).hex()`) and identical on this emit and the same invocation's `pair_rail_case`, so the /ceo-boot deficit pairs a specific expected with its OWN case — counting (even (session, file-hash)-bucketed) cannot: an old completed case for the SAME (session, file) offset a later dead expected 1:1. An EXPECTED `review_id` with no matching `pair_rail_case` in-window = an outstanding (dead) review -> RED; off-shape COERCED to empty; empty falls back to the bucket-count heuristic (best-effort, pre-land events only — post-land every review carries an id)), `timeout_ms` (int 0..6000000 — ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6: the EFFECTIVE POST-CLAMP codex budget the paired review runs under, in integer MILLISECONDS, NOT float seconds; canonical_json no-float invariant, same encoding as `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms` — divide by 1000 to recover seconds; off-shape/NaN/inf/bool COERCED to 0 = "unknown budget", bounded in the typed wrapper AND re-coerced in the `emit_generic` dispatch branch. Carried on the DENOMINATOR as well as the case so the pair records the budget it ran under even when the case never arrives — see the `pair_rail_case` row for the §4(i) rationale and for why the integer encoding is load-bearing), `session_id` (explicit required kwarg on the typed emitter — the hook threads the PreToolUse event's own session id, no silent default), `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-161 W2 C5 / CF-9 (2026-07-27) — canonical-edit review ENTERED marker, emitted by `check_pair_rail.py:_decide()` only after the kill-switch / non-write-tool / not-L3+ / sentinel-bypass arms have all returned (those paths emit NOTHING). The durable session-correlated DENOMINATOR for the /ceo-boot `pair_rail` activity-conditioned liveness row: a window session with expected-but-no-outcome is the S254 dead-rail class and escalates RED; zero expected + zero outcomes is vacuously green; a healthy outcome from session B never masks session A. Typed emitter `emit_pair_rail_review_expected`; dedicated deny-by-default `_PAIR_RAIL_REVIEW_EXPECTED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + closed-enum coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: file paths, proposed content, any review text. NO ATLAS technique (liveness telemetry, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:489:| `directory_added_recorded` (v2.53) | `action`, `source` (str — CLOSED enum: `slash_command` / `register_repo_root` / `session_start_snapshot` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed — the CC 2.1.220 wire carries only the first two; `session_start_snapshot` is RESERVED for the documented --add-dir-at-LAUNCH blind spot: the launch flag never fires DirectoryAdded, so a SessionStart roots snapshot is the only producer that can record those roots without a second kernel-file ceremony), `directory_hash_prefix` (str — EXACT 12-lowercase-hex sha256 prefix of the ABSOLUTE directory path, or exactly ""; bounded shape `([0-9a-f]{12})?`, RAW value validated — off-shape incl. oversize DROPPED to "", never truncated; the raw path is FORBIDDEN on the wire per the LLM06 side-channel guard and lives ONLY in the gitignored `.claude/state/session-roots.json` registry), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-163 T3.1 / ADR-183 (2026-07-28) — POST-FACTO forensic record that the session's write surface grew, emitted by `check_directory_added.py` (the DirectoryAdded observer-WRITER; the event is NOTIFICATION-ONLY on CC 2.1.220 — permission/sandbox already include the dir BEFORE dispatch, so no emit here ever claims prevention). Typed emitter `emit_directory_added_recorded`; dedicated deny-by-default `_DIRECTORY_ADDED_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + closed-enum VALUE coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the raw directory path, registry contents. NO ATLAS technique (perimeter observability, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:490:| `notification_lifecycle` (v2.53) | `action`, `notification_type` (str — CLOSED enum: `agent_needs_input` / `agent_completed` / `permission_request` / `other`; the harness enum is OPEN (matcher-visible string), so any unrecognized wire value is COERCED to `other` and the raw type string is NEVER echoed into the signed chain), `has_title` (bool), `message_sha256_prefix` (str — EXACT 12-lowercase-hex sha256 prefix of the notification message body, or exactly "" for empty/absent; bounded shape `([0-9a-f]{12})?`, RAW value validated — off-shape incl. oversize DROPPED to "", never truncated; hash, never content — a notification message can quote tool output, file paths, or secrets), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-163 T3.2 / ADR-183 (2026-07-28) — Notification lifecycle telemetry feeding agent liveness, emitted by `check_notification.py` (pure observer: stdout always `{}` exit 0; kill-switch `CEO_NOTIFICATION_TELEMETRY=0` checked before stdin read; empty payload short-circuits without a vacuous row). Typed emitter `emit_notification_lifecycle`; dedicated deny-by-default `_NOTIFICATION_LIFECYCLE_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + closed-enum VALUE coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: `message`/`title` TEXT (no-value-echo). NO ATLAS technique (liveness telemetry, not a detection signal). |
