SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:503:| `spawn_tool_scope_violation` (v2.41) | `action`, `session_id`, `rail` (str — CLOSED enum: `tool_scope` / `depth` / `overlap` / `other`), `enforced` (int 0/1 — coerced), `detail` (str — tool-NAMES + counts only; paths are 12-hex sha256 prefixes), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-133 E3 (Goose-harvest) — spawn-rail tool-scope violation breadcrumb. Routes through the dedicated dispatch-gate branch + `_SPAWN_TOOL_SCOPE_VIOLATION_ALLOWLIST` (built on `_OPTIMIZER_ENVELOPE`). DENIED on the wire: raw path / prompt / tool-arg bodies. NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
